WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:03.534
-Our first guest is a two-time
Emmy winner starring in

00:00:03.534 --> 00:00:06.267
the third and final season of
his popular series,

00:00:06.267 --> 00:00:08.534
"After Life,"
which is on Netflix now.

00:00:08.534 --> 00:00:11.834
Here's the always entertaining
Ricky Gervais!

00:00:11.834 --> 00:00:13.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.534 --> 00:00:16.501
Ah! Look at Ricky Gervais!

00:00:16.501 --> 00:00:18.434
Come on!
-Hello.

00:00:18.434 --> 00:00:21.868
-You look good, buddy.
You look happy.

00:00:21.868 --> 00:00:25.467
-Well, yeah, I'm drinking beer.

00:00:25.467 --> 00:00:27.033
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:27.033 --> 00:00:30.000
Okay, good, that's probably what
it is.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.133
Are you excited
about the new year?

00:00:32.133 --> 00:00:35.334
Here we are in January 2022.

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:38.000
-Yeah. Yeah, I'm really excited.
Yeah.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.501
What do you mean? Why?
Well, yeah.

00:00:40.501 --> 00:00:42.667
-Last time we talked about
you getting into shape

00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:44.601
and you said that --
-Yeah.

00:00:44.601 --> 00:00:47.300
-Yeah, you said you're kind of
not doing that anymore.

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:50.000
-Well, I am. I decided to --

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.701
I did try to get in --
I have been working on my body.

00:00:52.701 --> 00:00:56.467
And traditionally, you know,
you're meant to sort of gain

00:00:56.467 --> 00:00:59.334
muscle and lose fat,
but I went the other way.

00:00:59.334 --> 00:01:00.834
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.834 --> 00:01:05.667
So I've managed to bulk up
but with putting on

00:01:05.667 --> 00:01:07.801
eight pounds of pure fat
around my middle.

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:09.767
[ Laughter ]
I was worried I was getting

00:01:09.767 --> 00:01:11.868
too svelte and too handsome,

00:01:11.868 --> 00:01:14.234
and I was worried it would
interfere with my comedy,

00:01:14.234 --> 00:01:16.567
so I went that way.
-Smart.

00:01:16.567 --> 00:01:18.734
-So yeah, I'm looking great.

00:01:18.734 --> 00:01:21.467
I'm in great shape,
the shape being a sphere.

00:01:21.467 --> 00:01:24.133
[ Laughter ]
But I'm in great shape, yeah.

00:01:24.133 --> 00:01:26.467
-I heard this -- I don't know
if this is true or recent --

00:01:26.467 --> 00:01:28.601
but did you throw your back out?

00:01:28.601 --> 00:01:32.100
-Yeah, it happens once or twice
a year.

00:01:33.534 --> 00:01:36.200
This time it was tying up
my shoelace.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:37.667
It's ridiculous.

00:01:37.667 --> 00:01:40.901
So, I go down, and I feel
something go and that's it.

00:01:40.901 --> 00:01:45.834
It's from an old injury that I
did about 30, 35 years ago.

00:01:45.834 --> 00:01:47.868
Me and Jane,
we didn't have any money.

00:01:47.868 --> 00:01:50.334
We'd saved up for
a little holiday.

00:01:50.334 --> 00:01:52.834
We had a week in Italy, okay?

00:01:52.834 --> 00:01:56.200
So we had a hotel, but it had a
tennis court, and I love tennis.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:02:00.234
And the first day, I was playing
this sort of coach there,

00:02:00.234 --> 00:02:02.934
and I was sort of showing off,
right?

00:02:02.934 --> 00:02:05.367
To show I was trying to win,
right?

00:02:05.367 --> 00:02:06.834
So I did this --
-The tennis pro.

00:02:06.834 --> 00:02:09.801
-And my back went, and I pulled
my vertebrae apparently.

00:02:09.801 --> 00:02:11.667
And I was screaming in agony.

00:02:11.667 --> 00:02:13.801
There was a crowd looking,
"What's up with that guy?"

00:02:13.801 --> 00:02:15.200
They couldn't speak English.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:16.934
They took me to the room, right?

00:02:16.934 --> 00:02:19.000
I laid on the floor
of the hotel, right?

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:23.601
And I was on the floor in agony
for like --

00:02:23.601 --> 00:02:25.234
I say three days.

00:02:25.234 --> 00:02:27.634
At one point,
one of the staff --

00:02:27.634 --> 00:02:29.501
she wasn't a doctor or nurse.

00:02:29.501 --> 00:02:31.133
I think she was just
on reception.

00:02:31.133 --> 00:02:33.000
She came up and injected me
with something.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:34.501
Just stuck a needle in my ass.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.501 --> 00:02:35.734
I don't know what it was,

00:02:35.734 --> 00:02:37.801
but I was in such pain, I went,
"Yeah, whatever."

00:02:37.801 --> 00:02:39.868
Right? And then, so --

00:02:39.868 --> 00:02:41.801
I was sleeping --
I wasn't sleeping

00:02:41.801 --> 00:02:43.634
'cause I was in agony --
but I was --

00:02:43.634 --> 00:02:45.000
I remember for like three days,

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.467
I was drinking beer
out of the mini bar.

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:49.400
So drinking a bottle of beer,

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:51.534
and then I couldn't
get to the toilet,

00:02:51.534 --> 00:02:54.434
so I was weeing in
the empty bottle, right?

00:02:54.434 --> 00:02:57.868
And Jane was sort of
emptying those out

00:02:57.868 --> 00:02:59.200
and bringing me a new one.

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:02.300
And at one point Jane picked up
one bottle and said,

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:04.434
"Can I leave that for a while?
It's still warm."

00:03:04.434 --> 00:03:07.534
[ Laughter ]
So that was our holiday.

00:03:07.534 --> 00:03:10.200
-I can't believe
she's still with you.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:11.701
I can't believe
she's still with you.

00:03:11.701 --> 00:03:12.834
Unbelievable.
-No.

00:03:12.834 --> 00:03:17.934
-Ricky, do you consider yourself
a hypochondriac?

00:03:17.934 --> 00:03:19.467
-Yeah. No, I am.

00:03:19.467 --> 00:03:21.033
Along with everything else
I've got.

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:22.734
Along with all
my other illnesses,

00:03:22.734 --> 00:03:25.367
I'm also a hypochondriac,
so that just adds to it.

00:03:25.367 --> 00:03:28.300
Yeah, I am. And the thing --
I don't worry about stuff

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:30.000
until I wake up
and I could have --

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:33.434
Like, I'd find a spot,
like, or a sore throat.

00:03:33.434 --> 00:03:35.801
And the first thing I do
is Google it, right?

00:03:35.801 --> 00:03:38.734
And the first five things, I go,
"Oh, that's fine, that's fine."

00:03:38.734 --> 00:03:41.534
Then I push my luck
and I scroll too much

00:03:41.534 --> 00:03:44.234
and it's like some rare disease
that you definitely die of,

00:03:44.234 --> 00:03:45.534
and I think I've got that.

00:03:45.534 --> 00:03:48.067
And I say to Jane --
She goes, "Go to the doctor,"

00:03:48.067 --> 00:03:49.167
and that makes it worse.

00:03:49.167 --> 00:03:50.467
And I don't go to the doctor.

00:03:50.467 --> 00:03:52.467
I just have all of these
ailments that I just --

00:03:52.467 --> 00:03:54.667
I try and --
I just want to get better.

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:58.133
Or you know -- it's too much --
I'm too busy.

00:03:58.133 --> 00:04:00.167
It's a boring hour, isn't it,

00:04:00.167 --> 00:04:01.834
going to the doctor,
an appointment.

00:04:01.834 --> 00:04:03.334
If there was a doctor
in my basement,

00:04:03.334 --> 00:04:05.067
I'd be down there every day.

00:04:05.067 --> 00:04:06.400
I'd be going,
"What do you think of this?

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:09.767
What do you think of that?
Is that bad, right?"

00:04:09.767 --> 00:04:12.300
-Where do you think
you got it from?

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:15.834
-I don't know.
My Nan was like this.

00:04:15.834 --> 00:04:20.834
For the last 20 years of her
life, my Nan would say things

00:04:20.834 --> 00:04:24.267
like, "Oh, I'm not long
for this world."

00:04:24.267 --> 00:04:28.267
You know, and, "Oh, I won't see
this Christmas."

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:29.901
But then one year she was right.

00:04:29.901 --> 00:04:32.167
[ Laughter ]
You know what I mean?

00:04:32.167 --> 00:04:36.868
So, I remember when I was a kid,
my gran was --

00:04:36.868 --> 00:04:38.968
We were watching on the news.

00:04:38.968 --> 00:04:41.701
There was a prison riot
in London.

00:04:41.701 --> 00:04:43.367
-Mm-hmm.
-And all the prisoners were

00:04:43.367 --> 00:04:46.868
on the roof, and they were
smashing it up and setting fire

00:04:46.868 --> 00:04:48.801
to it and throwing tiles
down at the guards

00:04:48.801 --> 00:04:50.167
and they couldn't do anything.

00:04:50.167 --> 00:04:52.868
And it was on the news.
We were watching it.

00:04:52.868 --> 00:04:56.400
And my gran went,
"Oh, they should be locked up."

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:58.334
[ Laughter ]

00:04:58.334 --> 00:05:02.334
-Yeah, it's a prison riot.
They are locked up.

00:05:02.334 --> 00:05:05.968
That's fantastic.
She's very funny.

00:05:05.968 --> 00:05:08.200
I want to talk about your show,
"After Life."

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:11.534
This is the third
and final season,

00:05:11.534 --> 00:05:13.767
and I loved
the last two seasons.

00:05:15.567 --> 00:05:17.400
It's a beautiful show.

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:18.501
-Thank you.

00:05:18.501 --> 00:05:19.734
-It's heartwarming.

00:05:19.734 --> 00:05:21.801
It's the number-one show
on Netflix.

00:05:21.801 --> 00:05:24.300
-Yeah, it's crazy, I mean --

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:25.801
-That's fantastic.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:25.801 --> 00:05:30.033
-Every year it just got bigger
and bigger and --

00:05:30.033 --> 00:05:31.334
I mean, that's the beauty of
Netflix,

00:05:31.334 --> 00:05:33.634
that people are joining
the party all the time.

00:05:33.634 --> 00:05:38.767
But the main thing about it was
the emotional response.

00:05:38.767 --> 00:05:41.834
Like, people would come up to me
after the first season --

00:05:41.834 --> 00:05:43.400
people would come up to me on
the street and say,

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:45.200
"Oh, I lost my brother
the week before."

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:47.133
"I lost my partner,"
"I lost my mother."

00:05:47.133 --> 00:05:51.033
And you sort of realized
that everyone was grieving,

00:05:51.033 --> 00:05:53.133
so I thought I should treat that
with respect

00:05:53.133 --> 00:05:55.467
and that's why he doesn't just
snap out of it.

00:05:55.467 --> 00:05:58.767
I mean, it's a dark subject,
it's a dark, sad subject,

00:05:58.767 --> 00:06:03.901
but people -- I think they like
seeing something of themselves

00:06:03.901 --> 00:06:07.100
on TV they haven't seen before,
even if it's the bad bit.

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:09.968
And people would say to me,
"Oh, that was me.

00:06:09.968 --> 00:06:11.868
That was me after I lost
my wife," or something.

00:06:11.868 --> 00:06:15.267
And I just -- It's been lovely,
the response.

00:06:15.267 --> 00:06:18.601
And it sort of created a little
club as well, like on Twitter,

00:06:18.601 --> 00:06:20.901
people helping each other
and telling their own stories.

00:06:20.901 --> 00:06:24.033
And that's been the best thing
about it for me.

00:06:24.033 --> 00:06:25.334
I should say it's a comedy.

00:06:25.334 --> 00:06:27.567
It's very out there and funny.

00:06:27.567 --> 00:06:30.934
It's just about a guy
who's lost his wife

00:06:30.934 --> 00:06:34.634
and he's trying to cope, and one
of his main coping mechanisms

00:06:34.634 --> 00:06:37.501
is that he's angry and says
anything he wants

00:06:37.501 --> 00:06:39.267
because he doesn't care about
the consequences

00:06:39.267 --> 00:06:41.100
because at the beginning,
he doesn't care about living.

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:44.000
So that's the funny bit --
he just, you know,

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:48.834
he bumps into people and just
says what he thinks of them.

00:06:48.834 --> 00:06:51.100
-I mean, it's very, like you
said, it's a dark subject,

00:06:51.100 --> 00:06:55.133
but it's also very -- there's
a hopeful message to this.

00:06:55.133 --> 00:06:59.834
-I think it's uplifting, and I
think that's the big theme.

00:06:59.834 --> 00:07:01.367
It asks the big question,

00:07:01.367 --> 00:07:04.534
"If you lose everything,
is life still worth living?"

00:07:04.534 --> 00:07:06.501
And the answer is yes.

00:07:06.501 --> 00:07:07.834
You just got to find something
to do.

00:07:07.834 --> 00:07:10.334
And he tries everything,
and it doesn't work.

00:07:10.334 --> 00:07:13.467
He tries drinks, drugs,
violence, insults.

00:07:13.467 --> 00:07:19.434
And what he realizes is that
the real superpower is kindness,

00:07:19.434 --> 00:07:22.300
and that's where he finds
himself.

00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:23.834
-His purpose.

00:07:23.834 --> 00:07:27.200
-He can help others, you know,
and he sticks around --

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:29.501
Even though he's in pain,
he thinks he can make the world

00:07:29.501 --> 00:07:32.868
a slightly better place,
so that's the big message, yeah.

00:07:32.868 --> 00:07:35.634
-I think I read somewhere that
they just donated

00:07:35.634 --> 00:07:38.167
a bunch of benches around --

00:07:38.167 --> 00:07:41.200
-Oh, yeah.
They put these sort of --

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:46.667
One of the big sort of iconic
scenes in "After Life" is

00:07:46.667 --> 00:07:50.534
I meet an older woman
in the graveyard,

00:07:50.534 --> 00:07:52.334
and she's grieving,
and we become friends.

00:07:52.334 --> 00:07:54.934
And it's about the kindness
of strangers,

00:07:54.934 --> 00:07:57.300
because they're in the same boat
and she's lost her husband.

00:07:57.300 --> 00:08:01.234
And she really helps him.

00:08:01.234 --> 00:08:05.634
And so they've donated
these benches,

00:08:05.634 --> 00:08:06.701
called Benches of Hope,

00:08:06.701 --> 00:08:08.667
because it's a line
from the show --

00:08:08.667 --> 00:08:09.834
"hope is everything" --

00:08:09.834 --> 00:08:11.100
and they've dotted them
around the country

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:13.567
so people can go and sit
and think about stuff.

00:08:13.567 --> 00:08:16.834
And, yeah, it's sponsored by
a charity as well.

00:08:16.834 --> 00:08:17.968
-I thought that was so cool.

00:08:17.968 --> 00:08:19.634
[ Applause ]

00:08:19.634 --> 00:08:21.167
Keep going, buddy.

00:08:21.167 --> 00:08:22.601
We love you.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:08:22.601 --> 00:08:25.133
Here's Ricky Gervais in the new
season of "After Life."

00:08:25.133 --> 00:08:26.300
Take a look.

00:08:28.467 --> 00:08:30.934
[ Air horn blows ]
-Aah!

00:08:30.934 --> 00:08:32.834
-[ Laughing ]

00:08:32.834 --> 00:08:37.067
Oh, my gosh! Oh, my gosh!

00:08:37.067 --> 00:08:40.200
Maybe life is still
worth living!

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:41.434
Oh, my gosh.

00:08:41.434 --> 00:08:43.100
-That's not funny, actually.
That could have --

00:08:43.100 --> 00:08:44.801
-Well, I disagree.

00:08:44.801 --> 00:08:46.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:47.234
-That is funny.

00:08:47.234 --> 00:08:48.467
Ricky Gervais, everybody!

00:08:48.467 --> 00:08:51.133
Season three of "After Life"
is on Netflix now.

